1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,182
I wrote that sentence.

2
00:00:02,082 --> 00:00:04,137
It's one of six lines in a text file,

3
00:00:04,587 --> 00:00:06,397
and those six lines have a shape,

4
00:00:06,847 --> 00:00:11,935
the same shape as every quest, every person and every place you'll write in this course.

5
00:00:12,835 --> 00:00:15,945
So today, we learn that shape once.

6
00:00:17,745 --> 00:00:20,488
This is the file your story lives in.

7
00:00:21,388 --> 00:00:23,660
The lines at the top start with two slashes,

8
00:00:24,110 --> 00:00:27,708
which makes them notes, and the game skips right over them.

9
00:00:28,608 --> 00:00:30,825
Everything else in here is a record,

10
00:00:31,275 --> 00:00:33,806
and a record is simply one thing in your story.

11
00:00:35,606 --> 00:00:38,063
There are five of them in this file right now,

12
00:00:38,513 --> 00:00:41,946
and by the time we finish today there'll be six.

13
00:00:43,746 --> 00:00:45,610
Start by finding the hashes.

14
00:00:46,510 --> 00:00:49,542
There are eight lines that begin with one,

15
00:00:49,992 --> 00:00:52,496
and every one of those lines is a heading.

16
00:00:54,296 --> 00:00:55,623
They all have the same shape:

17
00:00:56,073 --> 00:00:58,402
some hashes, then a space,

18
00:00:58,852 --> 00:01:00,853
then a name in square brackets,

19
00:01:01,303 --> 00:01:03,737
and then a key in round brackets.

20
00:01:04,637 --> 00:01:07,048
That's the link you learned in Lecture Four.

21
00:01:08,848 --> 00:01:11,699
Now, the hashes tell you what's inside what.

22
00:01:12,599 --> 00:01:14,663
One hash is the title of the whole file.

23
00:01:15,563 --> 00:01:17,146
Two hashes make a section,

24
00:01:17,596 --> 00:01:19,597
which is a drawer for one kind of record.

25
00:01:20,497 --> 00:01:22,824
Three hashes make a record,

26
00:01:23,274 --> 00:01:27,948
and four make a record that sits inside the record above it.

27
00:01:29,748 --> 00:01:32,272
So these two, with four hashes each,

28
00:01:32,722 --> 00:01:34,474
are the steps of First Contact.

29
00:01:36,274 --> 00:01:37,872
Let's take one apart.

30
00:01:38,772 --> 00:01:40,960
The heading gives it a name.

31
00:01:41,410 --> 00:01:43,225
Then comes what I'll call the fence:

32
00:01:43,675 --> 00:01:47,119
two lines of three hyphens, and everything between them.

33
00:01:48,019 --> 00:01:51,076
Inside the fence there's one fact on each line,

34
00:01:51,526 --> 00:01:54,008
a label, a colon, and a value.

35
00:01:54,458 --> 00:01:57,036
Those are fields, and they're what the game acts on.

36
00:01:57,936 --> 00:01:59,910
Below the fence is the body,

37
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:02,851
which is just a sentence for people to read.

38
00:02:04,651 --> 00:02:06,844
So that's heading,

39
00:02:07,294 --> 00:02:07,706
fence,

40
00:02:08,156 --> 00:02:08,943
body.

41
00:02:10,743 --> 00:02:13,608
You don't need to know what these four fields do yet,

42
00:02:14,058 --> 00:02:15,977
but have a look at the last one.

43
00:02:16,877 --> 00:02:18,541
It points at another record,

44
00:02:18,991 --> 00:02:20,748
and it does that with a key,

45
00:02:21,198 --> 00:02:23,705
because nothing ever points at a name.

46
00:02:25,505 --> 00:02:29,558
Now see if you can find the same three parts here.

47
00:02:30,458 --> 00:02:33,800
One line inside this fence has no colon, and that's allowed,

48
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:39,411
because the first line of a fence can be a single word that says what kind of record this is.

49
00:02:41,211 --> 00:02:42,932
And here, in a scan record,

50
00:02:43,382 --> 00:02:46,783
the body is two lines that each start with a percent sign.

51
00:02:47,683 --> 00:02:50,543
Each of those lines is one reading,

52
00:02:50,993 --> 00:02:54,406
and Science gets shown just one of them.

53
00:02:56,206 --> 00:02:58,964
A quest's name becomes its line in the quest list,

54
00:02:59,414 --> 00:03:02,018
and its body becomes the description beside it.

55
00:03:02,918 --> 00:03:05,300
A scan record's name isn't shown anywhere,

56
00:03:05,750 --> 00:03:07,731
because that one's just for you,

57
00:03:08,181 --> 00:03:09,680
and its body is the reading.

58
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:13,398
And a key is never shown at all,

59
00:03:13,848 --> 00:03:15,991
because a key is for the game.

60
00:03:17,791 --> 00:03:18,867
Here's the first edit,

61
00:03:19,317 --> 00:03:22,338
and I'm changing the words and nothing else.

62
00:03:23,238 --> 00:03:26,478
It all stays on one line, however long that line gets,

63
00:03:26,928 --> 00:03:29,760
and I'm not touching the heading or the fence.

64
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:33,436
Now I'll write one of my own.

65
00:03:34,336 --> 00:03:38,059
I start with three hashes at the left edge, and then one space.

66
00:03:38,959 --> 00:03:41,173
Next comes a name, and then a key,

67
00:03:41,623 --> 00:03:45,624
which is small letters and an underscore, with no spaces.

68
00:03:46,524 --> 00:03:49,409
Then three hyphens, to open the fence.

69
00:03:50,309 --> 00:03:54,387
Inside it I say whose reading this is, which is the derelict,

70
00:03:54,837 --> 00:03:58,439
and which tab it goes on, which is intel.

71
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:01,820
Three more hyphens close the fence,

72
00:04:02,270 --> 00:04:06,912
and then comes the body, which starts with a percent sign and stays on one line.

73
00:04:08,712 --> 00:04:09,977
So that's six lines in all.

74
00:04:10,877 --> 00:04:12,400
Now notice what I didn't do.

75
00:04:13,300 --> 00:04:15,581
I didn't put a space in front of the hashes,

76
00:04:16,031 --> 00:04:18,435
I didn't type anything after the last round bracket,

77
00:04:18,885 --> 00:04:23,110
and I didn't press the Tab key in front of a field.

78
00:04:24,910 --> 00:04:28,274
There are three easy ways to get this shape wrong.

79
00:04:29,174 --> 00:04:32,833
The first is leaving out the space after the hashes.

80
00:04:33,283 --> 00:04:35,156
Then it isn't a heading any more,

81
00:04:35,606 --> 00:04:39,388
and my six lines become six readings of the record above.

82
00:04:40,288 --> 00:04:42,527
The second is one field pushed in from the edge.

83
00:04:42,977 --> 00:04:45,044
That glues it to the line above,

84
00:04:45,494 --> 00:04:48,026
and now the reading belongs to nobody.

85
00:04:48,926 --> 00:04:52,277
And the third is two hyphens instead of three,

86
00:04:52,727 --> 00:04:55,812
which isn't a fence, so there are no fields.

87
00:04:57,612 --> 00:05:00,574
In all three cases the game shows no intel tab,

88
00:05:01,024 --> 00:05:04,461
and it doesn't stop to tell you.

89
00:05:05,361 --> 00:05:07,109
So when your record isn't in the game,

90
00:05:07,559 --> 00:05:09,081
look at its shape first.

91
00:05:10,881 --> 00:05:12,715
First I check that there are no squiggles,

92
00:05:13,165 --> 00:05:15,082
and then I run one command.

93
00:05:15,982 --> 00:05:19,510
I'm looking for a single word, and that word is clean.

94
00:05:20,410 --> 00:05:22,620
The next lecture is all about this command,

95
00:05:23,070 --> 00:05:27,243
and it would've caught all three of the mistakes I just showed you.

96
00:05:29,043 --> 00:05:30,780
There's one warning until then, though.

97
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:34,928
If I put one hash where there should be three,

98
00:05:35,378 --> 00:05:36,903
it still says clean.

99
00:05:37,803 --> 00:05:41,791
That's because with one hash this line is a title, not a record,

100
00:05:42,241 --> 00:05:43,517
so the game never reads it.

101
00:05:45,317 --> 00:05:47,361
Clean only means the checker found nothing,

102
00:05:47,811 --> 00:05:49,668
so count your hashes yourself.

103
00:05:51,468 --> 00:05:54,174
I click the handheld, and then Quests,

104
00:05:54,624 --> 00:05:56,098
and this is the Quest Log.

105
00:05:56,998 --> 00:05:59,883
There's my sentence, right beside First Contact.

106
00:06:00,783 --> 00:06:02,139
Now for the hulk.

107
00:06:02,589 --> 00:06:05,433
The ship scans it by itself once we're close enough,

108
00:06:05,883 --> 00:06:08,415
so there are three tabs here,

109
00:06:08,865 --> 00:06:11,096
and the second one is mine.

110
00:06:12,896 --> 00:06:15,794
Give the hulk a fourth tab, with a record of your own.

111
00:06:16,694 --> 00:06:19,066
Then change the name of First Contact,

112
00:06:19,516 --> 00:06:22,278
and watch what changes and what doesn't.

113
00:06:24,078 --> 00:06:26,851
Next time, we'll break five things on purpose,

114
00:06:27,301 --> 00:06:29,620
and read what the checker says.
